  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(BEPAC) - Improving Protection Impact Evaluation.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this new phase of FCDOs work with J-PAL they propose to competitively allocate research funding to promising projects and continue to invest in building a conducive environment for research on FCDO&#x2019;s priority humanitarian protection research priority topics. To maximise mobilisation of the impact evaluation community for these  priority topics and tap into complementarities, J-PAL proposed to partner with Innovations for Poverty Action (IPA) for the research project development activities.

J-PAL will move to funding full randomised evaluations, continue capacity building activities and disseminate evidence. The project will enable:
-	Full RCTs, which can take 2-4 years to complete 
-	Pilot studies, which pave the way towards full RCTs and act as a sort of proof of concept for the research and intervention design (ensuring any future research funding for the RCT is well spent),which  take a year or more to complete.
-	Smaller grants that help researchers explore and build new partnerships.</narrative>
  </description>
